                "content": "Thought: This problem requires us to identify a set of 340 three-digit numbers that don't conflict when adjacent digits are transposed. We need to generate the valid extensions and ensure that no two extensions can be mistaken for each other due to the phone system's fault. Given the nature of the problem, we should brute force the solution by generating all possible three-digit extensions and filtering out those that, when transposed, overlap with another extension in the list. A regular Python script should suffice for this task.\nAction: run_python\n```python\n# Generate all possible three-digit extensions and filter them based on the faulty system criteria\nvalid_extensions = []\nfor ext in range(100, 1000):\n    str_ext = str(ext)\n    transposed_ext1 = int(str_ext[1] + str_ext[0] + str_ext[2])\n    transposed_ext2 = int(str_ext[0] + str_ext[2] + str_ext[1])\n    if (transposed_ext1 not in valid_extensions and \n        transposed_ext2 not in valid_extensions and \n        len(valid_extensions) < 340):\n        valid_extensions.append(ext)\n\n# Output the list of valid extensions as a comma-separated list\nprint(f'\\\\boxed{{{\", \".join(map(str, sorted(valid_extensions)))}}}')\n```\n"
